{"1-5":{"people":[{"id":"javan-h3120g","name":"Javan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Japheth","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"father-of-timothy-g5095h","name":"father of Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"timothy-g5095g","name":"Timothy","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[{"id":"lystra-g3082","name":"Lystra","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"derbe-g1190","name":"Derbe","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"iconium-g2430","name":"Iconium","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4}],"words":[{"base":"G3082","lemma":"Λύστρα","tr":"Lustra","gloss":"Lystra","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"G1672","lemma":"Ἕλλην=Ἕλλην","tr":"Hellēn","gloss":"Greek, Gentile","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":194},{"base":"G5259","lemma":"ὑπό","tr":"hupo","gloss":"by","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":219},{"base":"G3962","lemma":"πατήρ","tr":"patēr","gloss":"father","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":413},{"base":"G1191","lemma":"Δέρβη","tr":"Derbē","gloss":"Derbe","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4732","lemma":"στερεόω","tr":"stereoō","gloss":"to strengthen","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1279","lemma":"διαπορεύω","tr":"diaporeuō","gloss":"to go through","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G1378","lemma":"δόγμα","tr":"dogma","gloss":"decree","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G2430","lemma":"Ἰκόνιον","tr":"Ikonion","gloss":"Iconium","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":9,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Then the church throughout Judea, Galilee, and Samaria experienced a time of peace. It grew in strength and numbers, living in the fear of the Lord and the encouragement of the Holy Spirit.","from":5},{"book":"GAL","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Yet not even Titus, who was with me, was compelled to be circumcised, even though he was a Greek.","from":3},{"book":"2TI","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"I am reminded of your sincere faith, which first dwelt in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice, and I am convinced is in you as well.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":2,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"praising God and enjoying the favor of all the people. And the Lord added to their number daily those who were being saved.","from":5},{"book":"1CO","chapter":9,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win the Jews. To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law.","from":3},{"book":"ACT","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So the word of God continued to spread. The number of disciples in Jerusalem grew rapidly, and a great number of priests became obedient to the faith.","from":5},{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The brothers immediately sent Paul to the coast, but Silas and Timothy remained in Berea.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3}]},"6-10":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[{"id":"asia-g0773","name":"Asia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"galatia-g1053","name":"Galatia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"phrygia-g5435","name":"Phrygia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"mysia-g3465","name":"Mysia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"bithynia-g0978","name":"Bithynia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"troas-g5174","name":"Troas","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9}],"words":[{"base":"G3465","lemma":"Μυσία","tr":"Musia","gloss":"Mysia","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G3705","lemma":"ὅραμα","tr":"horama","gloss":"vision","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G3109","lemma":"Μακεδονία","tr":"Makedonia","gloss":"Macedonia","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G0978","lemma":"Βιθυνία","tr":"Bithunia","gloss":"Bithynia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1054","lemma":"Γαλατικός","tr":"Galatikos","gloss":"Galatia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G4151","lemma":"πνεῦμα","tr":"pneuma","gloss":"spirit","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":379},{"base":"G1224","lemma":"διαβαίνω","tr":"diabainō","gloss":"to cross","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5435","lemma":"Φρυγία","tr":"Phrugia","gloss":"Phrygia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G3110","lemma":"Μακεδών","tr":"Makedōn","gloss":"Macedonia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G5174","lemma":"Τρωάς","tr":"Trōas","gloss":"Troas","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"After Paul had spent some time in Antioch, he traveled from place to place throughout the region of Galatia and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples.","from":6},{"book":"2CO","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,","from":8},{"book":"2TI","chapter":4,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When you come, bring the cloak that I left with Carpus at Troas, and my scrolls, especially the parchments.","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":9,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"In Damascus there was a disciple named Ananias. The Lord spoke to him in a vision, “Ananias!” “Here I am, Lord,” he answered.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":9,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"In a vision he has seen a man named Ananias come and place his hands on him to restore his sight.”","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"We sailed from Troas straight to Samothrace, and the following day on to Neapolis.","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And when Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul devoted himself fully to the word, testifying to the Jews that Jesus is the Christ.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"After these things had happened, Paul resolved in the Spirit to go to Jerusalem, passing through Macedonia and Achaia. “After I have been there,” he said, “I must see Rome as well.”","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"11-15":{"people":[{"id":"lydia-g3070","name":"Lydia","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"neapolis-g3496","name":"Neapolis","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"samothrace-g4543","name":"Samothrace","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"troas-g5174","name":"Troas","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"philippi-g5375","name":"Philippi","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"thyatira-g2363","name":"Thyatira","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"G4172","lemma":"πόλις","tr":"polis","gloss":"city","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":163},{"base":"G3624","lemma":"οἶκος","tr":"oikos","gloss":"house: home","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":113},{"base":"G1511","lemma":"εἶναι","tr":"einai","gloss":"to exist","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":124},{"base":"G1135","lemma":"γυνή","tr":"gunē","gloss":"woman","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":211},{"base":"G2980","lemma":"λαλέω","tr":"laleō","gloss":"to speak","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":294},{"base":"G2113","lemma":"εὐθυδρομέω","tr":"euthudromeō","gloss":"to sail straight","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G3070","lemma":"Λυδία","tr":"Ludia","gloss":"Lydia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G3849","lemma":"παραβιάζομαι","tr":"parabiazomai","gloss":"to urge","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","tr":"hēmera","gloss":"day","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":389},{"base":"G2363","lemma":"Θυάτειρα","tr":"Thuateira","gloss":"Thyatira","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":24,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"Then He opened their minds to understand the Scriptures.","from":14},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":22,"source":"openbible","text":"that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in your knowledge of Him.","from":14},{"book":"EPH","chapter":1,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":22,"source":"openbible","text":"I ask that the eyes of your heart may be enlightened, so that you may know the hope of His calling, the riches of His glorious inheritance in the saints,","from":14},{"book":"ISA","chapter":50,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"The Lord GOD has opened My ears, and I have not been rebellious, nor have I turned back.","from":14},{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"“No one can come to Me unless the Father who sent Me draws him, and I will raise him up at the last day.","from":14},{"book":"JHN","chapter":6,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"It is written in the Prophets: ‘And they will all be taught by God.’ Everyone who has heard the Father and learned from Him comes to Me—","from":14},{"book":"REV","chapter":3,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears My voice and opens the door, I will come in and dine with him, and he with Me.","from":14},{"book":"2CO","chapter":3,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"But their minds were closed. For to this day the same veil remains at the reading of the old covenant. It has not been lifted, because only in Christ can it be removed.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-24":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"silas-g4609","name":"Silas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"G5310","lemma":"ὕψιστος","tr":"hupsistos","gloss":"Highest","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13,"top":true},{"base":"G2039","lemma":"ἐργασία","tr":"ergasia","gloss":"work","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":158},{"base":"G4755","lemma":"στρατηγός","tr":"stratēgos","gloss":"officer","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"G1831","lemma":"ἐξέρχομαι","tr":"exerchomai","gloss":"to go out","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":216},{"base":"G2605","lemma":"καταγγέλλω","tr":"katangellō","gloss":"to proclaim","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"G4183","lemma":"πολύς","tr":"polus","gloss":"much","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":367},{"base":"G3853","lemma":"παραγγέλλω","tr":"parangellō","gloss":"to order","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":31},{"base":"G5438","lemma":"φυλακή","tr":"phulakē","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"G0906","lemma":"βάλλω","tr":"ballō","gloss":"to throw: throw","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"G3748","lemma":"ὅστις","tr":"hostis, hētis","gloss":"who","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":144}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":19,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"You must not turn to mediums or spiritists; do not seek them out, or you will be defiled by them. I am the LORD your God.","from":16},{"book":"MRK","chapter":16,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And these signs will accompany those who believe: In My name they will drive out demons; they will speak in new tongues;","from":18},{"book":"DEU","chapter":18,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"When you enter the land that the LORD your God is giving you, do not imitate the detestable ways of the nations there.","from":16},{"book":"DEU","chapter":18,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"casts spells, consults a medium or spiritist, or inquires of the dead.","from":16},{"book":"LUK","chapter":10,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"The seventy-two returned with joy and said, “Lord, even the demons submit to us in Your name.”","from":18},{"book":"LUK","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Behold, I have given you authority to tread on snakes and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will harm you.","from":18},{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Jesus answered, “I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.","from":17},{"book":"1TH","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"As you are aware, we had already endured suffering and shameful treatment in Philippi. But in the face of strong opposition, we were bold in our God to speak to you the gospel of God.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"25-34":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"silas-g4609","name":"Silas","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":31}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":158},{"base":"G4609","lemma":"Σίλας","tr":"Silas","gloss":"Silas","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G1198","lemma":"δέσμιος","tr":"desmios","gloss":"prisoner","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"G3916","lemma":"παραχρῆμα","tr":"parachrēma","gloss":"instantly","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"G2374","lemma":"θύρα","tr":"thura","gloss":"door","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":39},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G0455","lemma":"ἀνοίγω","tr":"anoigō","gloss":"to open","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":77},{"base":"G2962","lemma":"κύριος","tr":"kurios","gloss":"lord: God","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":714},{"base":"G4982","lemma":"σῴζω","tr":"sōzō","gloss":"to save","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":105},{"base":"G3624","lemma":"οἶκος","tr":"oikos","gloss":"house: home","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":113}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":1,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":35,"source":"both","text":"But to all who did receive Him, to those who believed in His name, He gave the right to become children of God—","from":31},{"book":"ACT","chapter":2,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":34,"source":"openbible","text":"Peter replied, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.","from":31},{"book":"ACT","chapter":2,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":34,"source":"both","text":"This promise belongs to you and your children and to all who are far off—to all whom the Lord our God will call to Himself.”","from":31},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"Rejoice at all times.","from":25},{"book":"1TH","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"Give thanks in every circumstance, for this is Godʼs will for you in Christ Jesus.","from":25},{"book":"JHN","chapter":3,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. Whoever rejects the Son will not see life. Instead, the wrath of God remains on him.”","from":31},{"book":"ROM","chapter":10,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"that if you confess with your mouth, “Jesus is Lord,” and believe in your heart that God raised Him from the dead, you will be saved.","from":31},{"book":"ROM","chapter":10,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"For with your heart you believe and are justified, and with your mouth you confess and are saved.","from":31}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"35-40":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"lydia-g3070","name":"Lydia","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":40}],"places":[{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":37}],"words":[{"base":"G4755","lemma":"στρατηγός","tr":"stratēgos","gloss":"officer","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":10},{"base":"G4465","lemma":"ῥαβδοῦχος","tr":"rhabdouchos","gloss":"police","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G1806","lemma":"ἐξάγω","tr":"exagō","gloss":"to lead out","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G4514","lemma":"Ῥωμαῖος","tr":"Rhōmaios","gloss":"Roman","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G1831","lemma":"ἐξέρχομαι","tr":"exerchomai","gloss":"to go out","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":216},{"base":"G0518","lemma":"ἀπαγγέλλω","tr":"apangellō","gloss":"to announce","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":43},{"base":"G5438","lemma":"φυλακή","tr":"phulakē","gloss":"prison","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"G0630","lemma":"ἀπολύω","tr":"apoluō","gloss":"to release: release","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":64},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":700},{"base":"G3870","lemma":"παρακαλέω","tr":"parakaleō","gloss":"to plead","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":109}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But as they stretched him out to strap him down, Paul said to the centurion standing there, “Is it lawful for you to flog a Roman citizen without a trial?”","from":37},{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"At once those who were about to interrogate Paul stepped back, and the commander himself was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen in chains.","from":37},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"strengthening the souls of the disciples and encouraging them to continue in the faith. “We must endure many hardships to enter the kingdom of God,” they said.","from":40},{"book":"ACT","chapter":16,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Among those listening was a woman named Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, who was a worshiper of God. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paulʼs message.","from":40},{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"At once those who were about to interrogate Paul stepped back, and the commander himself was alarmed when he realized that he had put a Roman citizen in chains.","from":38},{"book":"1TH","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith,","from":40},{"book":"1TH","chapter":3,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"so that none of you would be shaken by these trials. For you know that we are destined for this.","from":40},{"book":"EXO","chapter":4,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Moses went back to his father-in-law Jethro and said to him, “Please let me return to my brothers in Egypt to see if they are still alive.” “Go in peace,” Jethro replied.","from":36}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}